-- EXPECT-ERROR: Module `Sigil` does not export `r`
-- Sigils (widening slice 15, core-march.md §3). `~R"..."` parses fine (the
-- lexer accepts ANY single uppercase letter or lowercase identifier as a
-- SIGIL_PREFIX, lib/lexer/lexer.mll) and desugars to the general-case call
-- `Sigil.r(content')` (desugar.ml:669-680) -- but no `Sigil.r` exists in
-- stdlib/sigil.march, so the rejection happens at the ORDINARY qualified-
-- name-resolution step, not from any sigil-specific validation. This is the
-- honest proof that "every sigil types via (T-App) against its desugared
-- callee" cuts both ways: an unimplemented name is rejected the same way an
-- unbound qualified call always is. Accept companion: accept/t79 (`~toml`,
-- an implemented name, resolves and types cleanly).
mod Main do
  fn main() do
    let v = ~R"abc"
    println("ok")
  end
end
